####################################################################################################
#   
#   The *.CCPavg file is an output to check the CCP solver convergence
#   
#   sinV1     = self DC bias, in Volts   
#   sinVo     = AC component of RF source potential, in Volts
#   sinF      = freq of RF source potential, in Hz
#   Cb        = capacitance of the capacitor connecting RF source and sinusoidal BC   
#   
#   te_avg    = Electron temperature averaged over 1 RF cycle and whole plasma domain, in eV
#   ne_avg    = Electron density     averaged over 1 RF cycle and whole plasma domain, in 1/m**3
#   CCPpwr    = CCP power   (je*E)   averaged over 1 RF cycle for whole plasma domain, in Watts
#   Eloss     = Electron energy loss averaged over 1 RF cycle for whole plasma domain, in Watts
#   eP        = Electron             produced over 1 RF cycle for whole plasma domain, in #
#   neP       = Electron density     produced over 1 RF cycle for whole plasma domain, in #/m**3
#   
#   sum_fluxi = total ions number flux over 1 RF cycle for given boundary type, in #
#   sum_fluxe = total elec number flux over 1 RF cycle for given boundary type, in #
#   sum_flxee = total elec energy flux over 1 RF cycle for given boundary type, in Watts
#   Vsin*     = sinusoidal BC of number * 
#   Vfix      = fixed-V BC
#   Efix      = fixed-E BC
#   charge    = dielectric BC
#   
#   Please note if the ccp solution is stabilized, eP = SUM(sum_fluxe), and sum_fluxi = sum_fluxe   
#   
#   
####################################################################################################
    
 n_times =      100  sinV1 sinVo sinF = -0.1000E+02 0.1000E+03 0.2700E+08 delt_V1 capacitance = -0.1000E+02  0.3333E-08
 n_times =      100  CCPpwr  Ionpwr Totpwr =  0.1846E+03 0.7210E+02 0.2567E+03
 n_times =      100  te_avg ne_avg CCPpwr Eloss eP neP =  0.8440E+00 0.4935E+15 0.1846E+03 0.7936E-02-0.2415E+06-0.1956E+08
  BC type = Efix       charge     Vfix       Vsin1        sum(BCs) 
